sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS 1 (token minted at admission, vault) and R2-R4, swamp-tasks-model. docs/reference/tasks.md#publish-an-external-group.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rule 16 (no tip read: a push without force refuses a divergent tip and pushes nothing for an identical one); rule 22 (no shipped scripts: task VM work is `@swamp/ssh exec` argv, 209 work is inline `git` and `gh api`; one workspace check, since import checks the bundled commit and tree).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tasks:publish
  %% kind: tasks.publish
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Task VM<br/>reached over ssh
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  CLI->>GW: tasks:publish 42<br/>--check=17 --title=… --body=…
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit tasks:publish 42 --check=17 --title="Deliver the feature" --body="Adds the feature."`
  %%> - syntax: `[group] --check=ID [--title=TEXT --body=TEXT] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the task group, and the passed handoff check whose commit is published
  %%> - optionally a title and body together, to open or update the pull request; without them it only pushes
  Note over GW: Check the candidate<br/>task #5165 · mint push token
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to the Gateway
  %%> - group 42 is an open external group with its own task VM workspace
  %%> - check 17 passed for group 42, and required hosted CI passed on its commit, else `tasks.commit_not_checked`
  %%> - no other task runs on group 42; the Gateway holds one lock per group
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - captures the repository, default branch, commit, checked tree and the task VM's SSH target
  %%> - mints a token for that one repository with `contents: write`, `pull_requests: write` and `workflows: write`, and pushes it to the vault as `task-publish-5165` after commit (R3)
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5165 recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the commit, tree, branch `task-42`, default branch and the optional title and body
  %%> - the vault key name of the token, never the token
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5165
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Check the workspace<br/>HEAD + tree = check 17
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches the task VM over SSH from 209, with `@swamp/ssh exec` argv: `git read-tree HEAD`, `git add --all` and `git write-tree` on a per-run index file, then `git rev-parse HEAD`
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that HEAD and the whole working tree still equal the checked candidate; the real index is not touched
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a moved candidate: `tasks.head_moved`; nothing is pushed
  SW->>N: Export the commit<br/>git bundle · copy to 209
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - runs `git bundle create <file> HEAD` as one `@swamp/ssh exec` argv and copies the file to 209 with `@swamp/ssh copy`
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the task VM never gets a GitHub token, and its Git configuration is never loaded
  Note over SW: Import into a bare repo<br/>scratch repository on 209
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - `git init --bare`, `git fetch` of the bundle and `git rev-parse` in one inline shell step on 209; only this repository uses the token
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a bundle whose HEAD or tree is not the checked candidate: `tasks.head_moved`
  SW->>GH: Push the branch<br/>git push task-42 · no force
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - pushes the checked commit to `task-42` without force, with the token from `vault.get`
  %%> - the token reaches Git only as an extra header in the environment, never in argv or run history
  %%> - an identical tip pushes nothing
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a divergent tip: git refuses the push by itself, mapped to `tasks.not_fast_forward`; no tip read runs first
  %%> - an installation without `Workflows` write when the commit changes `.github/workflows/`: `tasks.workflows_permission`
  opt with --title and --body
    SW->>GH: Open or update the PR<br/>task-42 → default branch
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - looks for an open pull request from `task-42` with `gh api`; updates its title and body when found, else opens one
    %%> - the title and body go to `gh api` on stdin, unchanged
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - no reviewers, no brief coverage, no board status change
  end
  SW->>GH: Revoke the token<br/>DELETE /installation/token
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - revokes the token with `gh api`, and removes the scratch files on the task VM and on 209, on success and on failure
  %%> If it fails:
  %%> - the run still reports its result; the token expires within one hour
  alt pushed
    GH-->>SW: PR #57 · head sha
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the branch, commit, and the PR number and URL, or null PR fields for a push alone
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event · PR
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the publication<br/>watch PR #57 · task done
    %%> Result:
    %%> - group 42 watches PR #57; its board status and settle metrics stay as they are
    %%> - task #5165 succeeds
  else a step fails
    GH--xSW: refused or no reply
    %%> When:
    %%> - the workspace moved, the tip diverged, the push or PR write was refused, or a reply was lost
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code, such as `tasks.push_failed`
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>group kept · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - task #5165 fails; group 42 and its workspace stay as they are
    %%> On GitHub:
    %%> - a push or PR that started stays; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again: a new task gets a new token; an identical tip pushes nothing, and the PR is looked up again before any write
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5165
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
